David Justiss wrote:
> I just downloaded Angband recently, and played a couple games.  So
> far it seems kinda boring compared to Nethack.

Angband is very combat-oriented.  In fact, it's 100% combat -
everything else is in support of that.  The only thing to do in the
game is kill monsters.  You also look for better gear and shop, but you
only do those things to kill monsters more efficiently ;)  The combat
and combat-magic side of the game is very detailed - 9 spell books (of
9 spells each) for each type of caster, many different types of weapons
and enchantments, various buffing spells, spectrum of resistances, etc.
 However, it is a purely (perhaps the ultimate extreme of a)
kill-the-monster game.  It certainly doesn't have the depth of gameplay
or the rich array of objects, interactions, etc. that NH has.

Some of the variants (e.g., ToME, Zangband, etc., or sister games like
ADOM) have more roleplaying/non-combat focus.

>    yes. how're you gonna dig through rock with your hands? Can you dig
> through walls in Angband without a tool?

Yes, you can use your sword or whatever if you're strong enough.
Usually you use a shovel or pick.  Early on, it's to get cash, though
killing monsters is better.  Later, you need to tunnel around vaults to
find their openings.

